      "tips": [
        {
          "text": "Maintain your composure at all times.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "text": "I would recommend doing codeforces and leetcode contests as much as you can.",
          "category": "Coding preparation",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "text": "Be 110% confident in yourself, chances are that then they will perceive you at 70%. (But please justify it too)",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "text": "I never made my introduction good to catch attention, I was only speaking about what I did. No one is interested in what you did. You need to communicate what you can do that can benefit them.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "text": "Don't let any incorrect answer derail your confidence.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "text": "Be humble. Placements are a humbling experience. The earlier you accept it, the easier it gets for you.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "text": "Communicate your thoughts well, and remember it is a two way street.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "text": "Have a good resume such that it looks filled completely, leaving any empty whitespaces signals that you haven’t done anything and memorize your resume on your fingertips so that any keyword or any related keyword is known to you and you can talk about it for a good 2 minutes at minimum.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "text": "If you are short on time, I recommend you to look out on at least 25 common interview questions on each tech keyword you mention on your resume.",
          "category": "Technical preparation",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "text": "Practice speaking a lot.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 5
        },
        {
          "text": "Solving CF or LC contests can help with this.",
          "category": "Coding preparation",
          "page": 7
        },
        {
          "text": "Research the company very well before giving any interview.",
          "category": "Interview strategy",
          "page": 6
        },
        {
          "text": "Also have a look at the Companies Expert youtube for prepping on all those HR questions. HR questions sound stupid at first, but they are very psychological in nature. Understanding what questions mean to ask what is very very important.",
